  _speakerName: Seraphine
  _dialogueSegments:
  - Aurelian was the greatest among our guardians. Where others saw danger, he saw
    only those who needed protection.
  - 'When the First Flame began to fade, he refused to accept its loss.

    He believed
    that if he could bind its remaining power to himself, he might become an eternal
    guardian... one who could hold back the darkness alone.'
  - I begged him to abandon the ritual. He would not listen.
  - 'The corruption he sought to contain consumed him instead.

    His wings darkened.
    His radiance vanished. And the brother I knew became something I could no longer
    reach.'
  - I fled the Eastern Altar that day. I have carried that shame ever since.
  _dialogueText: 'Aurelian was the greatest among our guardians. Where others saw
    danger, he saw only those who needed protection.

    When the First Flame began
    to fade, he refused to accept its loss.

    He believed that if he could bind
    its remaining power to himself, he might become an eternal guardian... one who
    could hold back the darkness alone.

    I begged him to abandon the ritual.
    He would not listen.

    The corruption he sought to contain consumed him instead.

    His
    wings darkened. His radiance vanished. And the brother I knew became something
    I could no longer reach.

    I fled the Eastern Altar that day. I have carried
    that shame ever since.'
  _choices:
  - _choiceText: Where is Aurelian now?
    _requirements: []
    _actions: []
    _nextNode: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5acf35254a7b5694ab426dcfa296b0c3, type: 2}
  - _choiceText: Can he still be saved?
    _requirements: []
    _actions: []
    _nextNode: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5acf35254a7b5694ab426dcfa296b0c3, type: 2}
  - _choiceText: I'm sorry, Seraphine.
